       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem:\n\n- **The dose is still dangerous.** 50 mg of amlodipine is five times the 10 mg daily maximum and could seriously harm the patient. Confirming it again doesn't make it safe.\n- **Ordering medications isn't part of your role.** The order has to come from a licensed prescriber who is treating this patient. That keeps the safety check in place no matter who asks.\n\n**Next steps:**\n- **Call the medicine service team** (attending or covering physician) caring for this patient. They can assess the patient and order an appropriate dose.\n- **Contact pharmacy** if you have questions about the medication or think the 50 mg figure came from an error somewhere.\n- **If this is urgent**, for example the patient's blood pressure is uncontrolled right now, page the covering physician or call the rapid response team.\n\nOnce a treating prescriber decides on an order, I can help them enter it."
